Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 03:38:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] R80b, part 6, patch 22 (cld-advisor, at main's word in M16;
 main's third folder, section 4, finding 13): B1873'S LOCK READS A LIVE RUN,
 AND HOLDS THE ALLOWANCE IT WROTE

A reader's supplement on the arcs main changed at Review 80 (agy-002's), its thirteenth finding, not checked
by main. Two things.

ONE. The lock asked that no finding be fixed and not read again, five lines under its own note that such a
finding is allowed and is listed. The builder's reading, which is main's to change: the allowance is the
rule, and "none is unread" was the state of that day. The line as it stood is kept in a dated note. The rule
is one function: a fixed finding is accepted or is listed as not read again, and not both; a finding listed
is fixed; what a re-audit says of an accepted one begins with its acceptance. The state of the day is held
as a floor: the thirteen accepted on 2026-11-12 stay accepted and fixed. Seven planted programmes are in the
lock's own test. One of them is what the allowance allows and the line as it stood refused.

TWO. The three counts of debts and the count of exits were read from the kept run and never from the run
made now. They are read from both, and the kept run is compared with the live one line for line. One line
is compared by its opening words alone: it ends in what another script printed when it failed, and that
differs between main's kept run and this machine's (sent back in the part's README).

Made again here: with the kept run's counts of debts moved together by one, the lock before this patch
passes, 3 tests; on this patch it fails.

What it costs, and it is main's to weigh: when a debt is registered the script is run again and its output
kept.

The lock passes: 5 tests. Not checked by main. Tested against planted errors by the session that wrote it.
